  "description": "To feed the hordes, doña María used to make her torta de elotes in a large, deep, rectangular baking dish, which I suspect was actually a medium-sized roasting pan. It was thick, dense, and hearty; an edible corn brick that tasted of earthy white corn and pungent cheese.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr 25 min.\n\nOptional substitutions: Mexican-style crema → sour cream; queso duro → haloumi",
  "author": [
    "María del Mar Cuadra"
  ],
